  "question": {
    "text": "The equation of tangent to the curve \\(y=\\sin x\\) at the point \\((\\pi, 0)\\) is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\\(x+y=0\\)",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\\(x+y=\\pi\\)",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\\(x-y=\\pi\\)",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\\(x-y=0\\)",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "\\(y=\\sin x \\Rightarrow \\frac{d y}{d x}=\\cos x \\Rightarrow\\left(\\frac{d y}{d x}\\right)_{(\\pi, 0)}=-1\\)\nTherefore the equation of tangent at \\((\\pi, 0)\\) is given by\n\\(y-0=-1(x-\\pi) \\Rightarrow x+y=\\pi\\)"
  }
}